# ESM Imports

This project uses `"type": "module"` in `package.json`. Node, Quokka, and Wallaby require explicit file extensions in relative imports.

## Rules

- Always include the `.js` extension in relative imports, even when importing from `.js` source files
- Use `import` / `export` only — no `require()`
- Prefer named imports over default imports when both exist

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — fails at runtime in Node ESM
import { pipe } from '../../utils/helpers';
import { ParseError } from './errors';

// ✅ GOOD
import { pipe } from '../../utils/helpers.js';
import { ParseError } from './errors.js';
```

When adding a new file, update every import path that references it to include `.js`.
